// Day 27: Confirm Entra ID sign-in logs are reaching Microsoft Sentinel
//
// What it looks for: the last day of interactive sign-ins in SigninLogs, one row per sign-in Id
// (arg_max keeps the latest record for each Id), with the fields that matter in an identity
// investigation: who, which app, from where, the result code, and the Conditional Access status.
//
// Why it matters: with Entra ID connected, a blocked sign-in, a failed MFA, or a sign-in from an
// unexpected country can be queried and correlated in Sentinel next to endpoint and email data,
// instead of being visible only in the Entra admin center.
//
// Result in my lab (Oct 10, 2026): 3 rows.
//   Robert Smith   One Outlook Web  JP  ResultType 53003  Access blocked by Conditional Access  failure
//   Richard Hale   One Outlook Web  US  ResultType 50140  "Keep me signed in" interrupt          success
//   my admin acct  Office365 Shell  US  ResultType 0                                           notApplied
// The 53003 row is the Day 25 block-by-country policy working, now visible from Sentinel.
SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1d)
| summarize arg_max(TimeGenerated, *) by Id
| project TimeGenerated, UserDisplayName, AppDisplayName, IPAddress, Location, ResultType, ResultDescription, ConditionalAccessStatus
| sort by TimeGenerated desc
